WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.430
Forty-five metres up, a phone
slips off the edge of a tower.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.680
It falls.

3
00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.200
A stopwatch starts, and
a speed readout climbs.

4
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.140
So when does it hit the ground,
and how fast is it going?

5
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.040
Does it just fall at a steady nine
point eight metres per second?

6
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.130
In this mission, you'll model it as
a particle with no air resistance:

7
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.510
constant acceleration g, nine point eight
metres per second squared, downwards.

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.730
You'll read velocity-time graphs, where
the gradient is the acceleration and the

9
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.240
area underneath is the displacement.

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.970
And you'll build the five
suvat formulae from that graph.

11
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.720
Your mission: work out
when the phone lands,

12
00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.480
and how fast it is going.
